  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Crafting Conditionals with Flowcharts\r\n\r\nExplore the flowchart elements that are provided in the sketch on this level. Then create a flowchart using the symbols provided to model a decision-making process of something that is personally relevant in your life.\r\n\r\nUse the example provided to help you get started and then delete it when you are down so you can save your version.\r\n\r\n:::details [Why use a flowchart?]\r\nWe map out our code using flowcharts so we can see our logic clearly and spot mistakes early. It’s like consulting a map before taking a road trip — you plan the “if this, then that” paths so you don’t get lost in your code. Flowcharts make your thinking visible and helps save time debugging later.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n\r\n### Save your image\r\nWhen you are done, **export your image** as a .png - it will be uploaded in the next level to help build the webpage. \r\n\r\n:::details [How to save]\r\n- Click on the stacked bars on the top left\r\n![](https://images.code.org/26fd4302afea23d437fb853b77372714-image-1761155648521.png)\r\n- Select `export image` and then `save as .png`\r\n- Name your file and move it to the location of your choice \r\n\r\n:::",
